  {
    "episode_id": 88120,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88120.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Well, a thing I focused on throughout my time in Congress is our budget and spending. I'm the most physically conservative member of Congress and have been over the last 10 years. And there are a couple other members who are pretty good, but most of the other ones are not very good at this. We're spending money like crazy, and none of it's balanced, of course, with any offsets or anything else. And that's continuing under Donald Trump, and it will continue under Joe Biden. So I'm going to make sure that we get our budget in order, that we're not spending crazy amounts of money on anything. I mean, look at military spending even over the past decade. It went up under Barack Obama. It's going up under Donald Trump. Do we need a strong military, of course? And we can have a strong military. We'd still have way more spending on our military if it weren't going up, you know, a couple hundred billion dollars like it's been going up over the past several years. And we focus on the wrong things with our military too. Let's have money go to the people who need the resources, the troops. Instead, we're wasting it on wars that are unnecessary or building bases overseas that we don't even use. So that's an important issue for me. And, you know, I've segued into the second topic as war. It's not okay for wars to go on for 20 years, like we're seeing in Afghanistan. It's not okay to use an authorization from 2001 and say, oh, we're just going to keep this war going on forever. Congress has to reassert its authority over war, and it has to respect the rights of the people. The people have to have a say in this. And I will make sure that Congress does its job. I'm not going to allow these wars to continue without Congress asserting itself. If Congress wants to continue a war, then it better take a vote and send an authorization to my desk. So that's really important. And then third, I would focus on things related to our rights, civil liberties, civil asset forfeiture, criminal justice reform, privacy, These are all issues I care a lot about. I've fought against the surveillance state. I've fought to protect people's property rights. You know, it's not okay for someone to be stopped and then have their property taken from them without any conviction, without any real due process. And that's what happens under civil asset forfeiture. And you have President Trump who has expanded it. And Joe Biden is someone who has been on the wrong side of all of these issues, basically. on criminal justice, on civil asset forfeiture, on privacy. He's been on the wrong side of all of it. So we need someone who's going to go in there and protect people's rights, and that's what I intend to do.",
