    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 88120,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88120.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, no, I have always pushed for more competition in elections. I think more competition really holds elected officials and those running for office accountable. I do want to ask you a couple of questions, one of which is a question that I'm hearing from a lot of libertarians, some independents, and people, especially in New York state who watched the last gubernatorial election. And that question is, as a libertarian running for president you're going to have to have a vice presidential candidate and would you consider Larry Sharp as that vice presidential candidate?",
