    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88120.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "I get the federal government out of education. I've co-sponsored legislation to abolish the Department of Education at the federal level. Sometimes people hear that and they say, well, there's not going to be any Department of Education anymore. We're talking about the federal Department of Education. There are still state departments of education. And while I think the best education decisions are made closest to home, people in states can make decisions about their education system. And it doesn't have to be at the federal level. And the problem with having it at the federal level is it doesn't help students. It doesn't help our education system. All that happens is money is funneled into DC. It's spread around among a bunch of bureaucrats. Then they write some rules and they attach some strings. And then they send a portion of the money back to the state. And now your whole education system is mired with these federal rules. And they'd also ties up teachers with a bunch of federal rules. So it hurts teachers. And then you get pennies on the dollar back and your whole system is recreated in the image of the federal government. And I don't think that's okay. And we're talking about only 10% of education spending anyways. Like here in the state of Michigan, 90% of the funding is from the state. 10% roughly is from the federal government.",
