    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88120.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 89,
    "turn_text": "You know, there's the Andy show every day around 12 noon where Cuomo goes on with his interminable lectures with the condescending attitude that he always has. I just could not help but notice, and one of my coworkers here at the station noticed, Andy's got a fresh haircut. And I don't know about you. The last haircut I had was in early March. And I'm starting to look like the station sheep dog Alfie these days. And this is to provide counterpoint to this whole thing. We have this hairdresser in Dallas, the Shelley Luther. I don't know if you've followed this story. She hasn't been able to, you know, her salon has been ordered closed. And anyway, she was slapped with fines and then a restraining order from the city of Dallas. Now this is in Texas, ladies and gentlemen, which is definitely a red state. Now she has been jailed by this arrogant judge. He has thrown her in the clink for seven days for trying to run her business because literally her hairstylists on her staff are going hungry so their kids can eat. And so just I want everybody to remember, you know, we get all in digging about this stuff when it happens and then we tend to forget about it. Don't forget about this. Everybody, remember November when you get to that ballot box. Don't reelect these jerks.",
