  {
    "episode_id": 88120,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88120.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 90,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, yeah. You know, and one of the things I think is really important to emphasize here is that government control is obviously too heavy-handed, right? We know that. That's clear. But a lot of these industries identified the risk and found a way to carry things out. socially or not just socially but safely in a safe way that really minimizes risk now you could look at people have face shields people have masks people are sanitizing between things and it really comes down to consent if you're a low risk individual and you're interacting with another low risk individual and you know and understand that they might have the virus and they might have no symptoms and they may be infectious, but you as an adult voluntarily make that decision to interact with an individual? That should be up to your right. That should be your choice. And I'm not saying this to say that we should be insensitive to people who are afraid. And I'm not saying that we should be cavalier with people who are at high risk. What I'm saying is people who are at high risk should make the decision to not interact with people who they think would bring risk to them. And I think that they're making those decisions themselves. You know, people are choosing not to see their grandchildren. They're choosing not to go shopping. They're relying on door delivery or somebody else to shop on their behalf. Anyways, Um, and people at lower risks are going and shopping at places like Wegmans and Aldes and Walmart and other stores like that. Um, people are doing it anyways. The only thing that is really happening here is government saying, I know better than you. I'm taking away your ability to consent. And I'm telling you where you can and cannot go. That there's literally the only differences going on here.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_04",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
