      },
      {
        "text": "Government control is too heavy-handed.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Consent should determine personal interactions involving potential infection risk.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Low-risk individuals can voluntarily choose to interact with others even if asymptomatic carriers exist.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The core difference in current policies lies in the replacement of individual consent with state-imposed rules.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Many industries recognized health risks and implemented safety measures.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "High-risk individuals should decide independently whether to avoid contact with potentially infected persons.",
