  {
    "episode_id": 88120,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88120.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 91,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, you know, and in this connection, by the way, I would like to steer everybody to a piece that's in the Democrat and Chronicle E edition. There's an article there which is entitled Behind the Protests There Are Two Americas. And this caught my attention because it was written by Glenn Harlan Reynolds, who's a professor at my law school, where I went to University of Tennessee Law School. It's a special to us a today and again the title is behind the protest. There are two Americas so basically what he's pointing out what Glenn's pointing out is the There's some starting to be some cracks that are starting to starting to appear Between the two Americas on the one hand we have the ruling elites the technocrats the people who have got life covered no matter what happens anyway and they are lecturing You know, the little people, people like you folks listening to the radio right now or I suppose presumably Andrew and me about how we need to live and how we need to endure privation and how we need to just put on this happy face that is prescribed to us by mass media, which of course has become essentially an arm of a propaganda arm of the status. And we're getting mad about it. And this is not going to end well. So you need to really start rattling the cages of these elected officials and telling them that their day is coming.",
